# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum-HPC integration challenge {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"
msgstr "Cabaran integrasi kuantum-HPC {#the-quantum-hpc-integration-challenge}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-performance computing (HPC) workflows often require seamless coordination between classical compute clusters and quantum processing units (QPUs). Different quantum hardware backends and services expose distinct authentication mechanisms, wire formats, and job lifecycle APIs. Integrating IBM Quantum systems into HPC workload managers (such as Slurm) requires a clean, standard interface for resource acquisition, job execution, and session management.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja pengkomputeran berprestasi tinggi (HPC) selalunya memerlukan penyelarasan yang lancar antara kelompok pengkomputeran klasik dan unit pemprosesan kuantum (QPU). Backend dan perkhidmatan perkakasan kuantum yang berbeza mendedahkan mekanisme pengesahan, format wayar, dan API kitaran hayat kerja yang berbeza. Mengintegrasikan sistem IBM Quantum ke dalam pengurus beban kerja HPC (seperti Slurm) memerlukan antara muka standard yang bersih untuk perolehan sumber, pelaksanaan kerja, dan pengurusan Session.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What QRMI is {#what-qrmi-is}"
msgstr "Apa itu QRMI {#what-qrmi-is}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** is a middleware library written in Rust that standardizes access to quantum hardware from HPC schedulers and classical applications. It exposes a single unified lifecycle API:\n"
msgstr "**Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)** ialah pustaka middleware yang ditulis dalam Rust yang menyeragamkan akses kepada perkakasan kuantum daripada penjadual HPC dan aplikasi klasik. Ia mendedahkan satu API kitaran hayat yang bersatu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QRMI is published as an open-source project at [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) and is described in the overview paper [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"
msgstr "QRMI diterbitkan sebagai projek sumber terbuka di [github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi) dan diterangkan dalam kertas gambaran keseluruhan [arXiv:2506.10052](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10052).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key design choices {#key-design-choices}"
msgstr "Pilihan reka bentuk utama {#key-design-choices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Resource lifecycle, not circuit compilation.** QRMI handles the acquire/submit/poll/release lifecycle and nothing else. Circuit compilation, optimization, and transpilation remain in the application layer (for example, Qiskit). This keeps the interface minimal and composable.\n"
msgstr "**Kitaran hayat sumber, bukan kompilasi Circuit.** QRMI mengendalikan kitaran hayat acquire/submit/poll/release dan tiada apa-apa lagi. Kompilasi Circuit, pengoptimuman, dan transpilation kekal di lapisan aplikasi (contohnya, Qiskit). Ini mengekalkan antara muka yang minimum dan boleh disusun semula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vendor portability model.** While QRMI provides common job-management calls (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) across supported hardware backends, changing vendors also requires different compilation passes, vendor-specific payload construction, and result decoding in the application layer.\n"
msgstr "**Model kebolehalihan vendor.** Walaupun QRMI menyediakan panggilan pengurusan kerja yang sama (`acquire`, `task_start`, `task_status`, `task_result`, `release`) merentasi Backend perkakasan yang disokong, menukar vendor juga memerlukan laluan kompilasi yang berbeza, pembinaan payload khusus vendor, dan penyahkodan hasil di lapisan aplikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Native IBM payload format.** For IBM Quantum backends, QRMI uses OpenQASM 3 JSON payloads (`QiskitPrimitive`) conforming to the Qiskit Runtime schema.\n"
msgstr "**Format payload IBM asli.** Untuk Backend IBM Quantum, QRMI menggunakan payload JSON OpenQASM 3 (`QiskitPrimitive`) yang mematuhi skema Qiskit Runtime.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Configuration through environment variables.** Credentials and endpoint URLs are read from environment variables at runtime. In an HPC cluster, the Slurm QRMI SPANK plugin sets these automatically when a job is dispatched. In a notebook or interactive session, you load them from a `.env` file. Application code never contains hardcoded credentials or endpoint URLs.\n"
msgstr "**Konfigurasi melalui pemboleh ubah persekitaran.** Kelayakan dan URL titik akhir dibaca daripada pemboleh ubah persekitaran semasa runtime. Dalam kelompok HPC, plugin SPANK QRMI Slurm menetapkan ini secara automatik apabila kerja dihantar. Dalam notebook atau sesi interaktif, anda memuatkannya daripada fail `.env`. Kod aplikasi tidak pernah mengandungi kelayakan atau URL titik akhir yang dikodkan keras.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**HPC scheduler integration through GRES.** When a Slurm job requests quantum resources using the QRMI SPANK plugin interface (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` and `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), the plugin injects `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` and `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` into the job environment. Applications call `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` to discover which resources were allocated &mdash; no hardcoded backend names required. `QRMIService` wraps this pattern for Qiskit users.\n"
msgstr "**Integrasi penjadual HPC melalui GRES.** Apabila kerja Slurm meminta sumber kuantum menggunakan antara muka plugin SPANK QRMI (`#SBATCH --gres=qpu:1` dan `#SBATCH --qpu=ibm_kingston`), plugin tersebut menyuntik `QRMI_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` dan `QRMI_JOB_QPU_TYPES` ke dalam persekitaran kerja. Aplikasi memanggil `get_job_qpu_resources_and_types()` untuk mengetahui sumber yang telah diperuntukkan &mdash; tiada nama Backend yang dikodkan keras diperlukan. `QRMIService` membungkus corak ini untuk pengguna Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The core API calls {#the-core-api-calls}"
msgstr "Panggilan API teras {#the-core-api-calls}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call | Purpose |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Acquire access to the resource (for example, opens a dedicated session); returns a lock token |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Retrieve backend capabilities (qubits, gates, coupling map) as JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Submit a quantum job; returns a job ID |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Poll job status (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Retrieve completed job results as a raw JSON string |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Cancel or clean up a job |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Release the resource lock (for example, closes the session) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Panggilan | Tujuan |\n"
"|------|---------|\n"
"| `qrmi.acquire()` | Memperoleh akses kepada sumber (contohnya, membuka sesi khusus); mengembalikan token kunci |\n"
"| `qrmi.target()` | Mendapatkan keupayaan Backend (Qubit, Gate, peta gandingan) sebagai JSON |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_start(payload)` | Menghantar kerja kuantum; mengembalikan ID kerja |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_status(job_id)` | Menyemak status kerja (`Queued`, `Running`, `Completed`, `Failed`) |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_result(job_id)` | Mendapatkan hasil kerja yang telah selesai sebagai rentetan JSON mentah |\n"
"| `qrmi.task_stop(job_id)` | Membatalkan atau membersihkan kerja |\n"
"| `qrmi.release(lock)` | Melepaskan kunci sumber (contohnya, menutup sesi) |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this tutorial covers {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"
msgstr "Apa yang diliputi oleh tutorial ini {#what-this-tutorial-covers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is structured in two parts:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini disusun kepada dua bahagian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Steps 1–3 (small-scale examples):** Introduce the QRMI API with a simple Bell state circuit demonstration on IBM Quantum hardware, covering direct low-level primitive usage as well as high-level `QRMIService` and `SamplerV2` integration.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1–3 (contoh skala kecil):** Memperkenalkan API QRMI dengan demonstrasi Circuit keadaan Bell yang mudah pada perkakasan IBM Quantum, merangkumi penggunaan primitif peringkat rendah secara langsung serta integrasi peringkat tinggi `QRMIService` dan `SamplerV2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Large-scale hardware example:** A complete SQD workflow for the N$_2$ molecule at a bond distance of 1.0 $\\AA$ (cc-pVDZ basis active space, 26 spatial orbitals / 52 qubits), executed on IBM Quantum hardware through QRMI. SQD combines quantum sampling of a LUCJ ansatz constructed with `ffsim` and self-consistent configuration recovery with `qiskit-addon-sqd`.\n"
msgstr "**Contoh perkakasan berskala besar:** Aliran kerja SQD lengkap untuk molekul N$_2$ pada jarak ikatan 1.0 $\\AA$ (ruang aktif asas cc-pVDZ, 26 orbital spatial / 52 Qubit), dilaksanakan pada perkakasan IBM Quantum melalui QRMI. SQD menggabungkan pensampelan kuantum ansatz LUCJ yang dibina dengan `ffsim` dan pemulihan konfigurasi swakonsisten dengan `qiskit-addon-sqd`.\n"

