# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale examples {#small-scale-examples}"
msgstr "Contoh skala kecil {#small-scale-examples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–3 introduce the QRMI API by using simple circuits. Each step maps to a core phase of the QRMI lifecycle against IBM Quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Langkah 1–3 memperkenalkan API QRMI dengan menggunakan Circuit yang mudah. Setiap langkah memetakan kepada fasa teras kitaran hayat QRMI terhadap perkakasan IBM Quantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payload for these initial steps is a small Bell state circuit chosen to be fast and inexpensive to run.\n"
msgstr "Payload untuk langkah-langkah awal ini ialah Circuit keadaan Bell kecil yang dipilih supaya pantas dan murah untuk dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These examples use hardware because they demonstrate remote resource allocation and job management. A local circuit simulator does not validate the QRMI service and scheduler integration. Running this notebook submits IBM Quantum jobs and requires access to the configured backend.\n"
msgstr "Contoh-contoh ini menggunakan perkakasan kerana ia menunjukkan peruntukan sumber jauh dan pengurusan kerja. Simulator Circuit tempatan tidak mengesahkan integrasi perkhidmatan QRMI dan penjadual. Menjalankan notebook ini menghantar kerja IBM Quantum dan memerlukan akses kepada Backend yang dikonfigurasikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map the classical problem to a quantum resource {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan masalah klasik kepada sumber kuantum {#step-1-map-the-classical-problem-to-a-quantum-resource}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first step in any QRMI workflow is to create a `QuantumResource` object and verify that it is accessible.\n"
msgstr "Langkah pertama dalam mana-mana aliran kerja QRMI ialah mencipta objek `QuantumResource` dan mengesahkan bahawa ia boleh diakses.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_target()` retrieves the backend's hardware description (qubit count, basis gates, coupling map) and packages it as a Qiskit `Target` object, which the transpiler uses in Step 2.\n"
msgstr "`get_target()` mendapatkan penerangan perkakasan Backend (bilangan Qubit, Gate asas, peta gandingan) dan membungkusnya sebagai objek `Target` Qiskit, yang digunakan oleh Transpiler dalam Langkah 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before submission, use Qiskit to transpile the circuit to the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA), using the `Target` object retrieved in Step 1.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum penghantaran, gunakan Qiskit untuk melakukan transpile Circuit kepada seni bina set arahan (ISA) Backend, menggunakan objek `Target` yang diperoleh dalam Langkah 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example then builds a `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, which wraps the OpenQASM 3 circuit string and job metadata into the IBM primitive schema.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini kemudian membina `Payload.QiskitPrimitive`, yang membungkus rentetan Circuit OpenQASM 3 dan metadata kerja ke dalam skema primitif IBM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using QRMI primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif QRMI {#step-3-execute-using-qrmi-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the payload built, the example submits the job and polls for completion. `task_start()` returns a job ID immediately; `task_status()` is polled until the status is no longer `Queued`/`Running`. Results are retrieved as a raw JSON string and parsed to extract measurement samples.\n"
msgstr "Setelah payload dibina, contoh ini menghantar kerja dan menyemak status sehingga selesai. `task_start()` mengembalikan ID kerja dengan serta-merta; `task_status()` disemak sehingga status tidak lagi `Queued`/`Running`. Hasil diperoleh sebagai rentetan JSON mentah dan dihuraikan untuk mengekstrak sampel pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cell keeps acquisition, execution, and cleanup together so that failures after acquisition still release a notebook-owned session.\n"
msgstr "Sel berikut mengekalkan perolehan, pelaksanaan, dan pembersihan bersama supaya kegagalan selepas perolehan tetap melepaskan sesi yang dimiliki oleh notebook.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Higher-level Qiskit interface: QRMIService and SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"
msgstr "Antara muka Qiskit peringkat tinggi: QRMIService dan SamplerV2 {#higher-level-qiskit-interface-qrmiservice-and-samplerv2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The raw lifecycle above provides explicit control over every call. For standard Qiskit workflows, QRMI provides a `SamplerV2` primitive implementing `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"
msgstr "Kitaran hayat mentah di atas menyediakan kawalan eksplisit ke atas setiap panggilan. Untuk aliran kerja Qiskit standard, QRMI menyediakan primitif `SamplerV2` yang melaksanakan `BaseSamplerV2`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Lifecycle management\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Pengurusan kitaran hayat\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`SamplerV2` handles payload serialization, submission (`task_start`), polling, and result decoding. In an HPC batch setting (for example, with Slurm), allocation and release are managed by the scheduler and the SPANK plugin. In an interactive Python session using direct low-level API objects, `acquire()` and `release()` can be used to explicitly manage dedicated sessions.\n"
msgstr "`SamplerV2` mengendalikan pensirian payload, penghantaran (`task_start`), penyemakan status, dan penyahkodan hasil. Dalam persekitaran kelompok HPC (contohnya, dengan Slurm), peruntukan dan pelepasan diurus oleh penjadual dan plugin SPANK. Dalam sesi Python interaktif yang menggunakan objek API peringkat rendah secara langsung, `acquire()` dan `release()` boleh digunakan untuk mengurus sesi khusus secara eksplisit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
